      "message": "nits: looping assert makes debug difficult since we can not know which one is failing from line number.\nI prefer the following code but this is up to you\n```\nassertTrafficStats(long rxBytes, long rxPackets, long txBytes, long txPackets,\n               Function\u003cInteger, Long\u003e fetcher) {\n   assertEquals(rxBytes, fetcher.apply(TrafficStats.TYPE_RX_BYTES));\n   assertEquals(rxPackets, fetcher.apply(TrafficStats.TYPE_RX_PACKETS));\n   assertEquals(txBytes, fetcher.apply(TrafficStats.TYPE_TX_BYTES));\n   assertEquals(txPackets, fetcher.apply(TrafficStats.TYPE_TX_PACKETS));\n}\n\nprivate void assertTrafficStatsValues() {\n   assertTrafficStats(rxBytes, rxPackets, txBytes, txPackets, (type) -\u003e mService.getTotalStats(type))\n   assertTrafficStats(rxBytes, rxPackets, txBytes, txPackets, (type) -\u003e mService.getIfaceStats(iface, type))\n   assertTrafficStats(rxBytes, rxPackets, txBytes, txPackets, (type) -\u003e mService.getUidStats(uid, type))\n}\n\n```",
